{"absent":["Locking, concurrency and ordering rules for programming counters, selectors or sampling buffers are not shown.","MSR access sequences, event scheduling, context switch handling and overflow or interrupt flows are not shown.","PEBS buffer allocation, threshold interrupt behavior and debug-store management are not shown.","IBS operation-side record layouts and fetch completion data beyond control bits are not shown.","Counter width handling, wraparound, privilege checks and virtualization mediation beyond capability flags are not shown.","No exported functions or cross-module callers beyond small inline index predicates are shown."],"dossier":"D10","findings":[{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_MAX_GENERIC","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_MAX_FIXED","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_FIXED","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::X86_PMC_IDX_MAX"],"text":"Generic counters are limited to 32, fixed counters to 16, fixed indices start at 32, and the total index space spans 64 entries."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_PERFCTR0","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_PERFCTR1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL0","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_FIXED_CTR_CTRL","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_FIXED_CTR0","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_FIXED_CTR1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_FIXED_CTR2","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_FIXED_CTR3"],"text":"Architectural MSR numbers are fixed: general counters at 0xc1 and 0xc2, event selectors at 0x186 and 0x187, fixed control at 0x38d, and fixed counters zero through three at 0x309 through 0x30c in order."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_EVENT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_UMASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_USR","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_OS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_EDGE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_PIN_CONTROL","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_INT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_ANY","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_ENABLE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_INV","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_CMASK"],"text":"The low event-select word packs an 8 bit event code plus an 8 bit unit mask, privilege and behavior flags for user, OS, edge, pin, interrupt, any-thread, enable and invert in bits 16 through 23, and an 8 bit compare mask in bits 24 through 31."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_BR_CNTR","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_EQ","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_RDPMC_USER_DISABLE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_UMASK2","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::HSW_IN_TX","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::HSW_IN_TX_CHECKPOINTED","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ICL_EVENTSEL_ADAPTIVE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ICL_FIXED_0_ADAPTIVE"],"text":"Extended event-select bits cover branch-counter logging at bit 35, equality mode at bit 36, user RDPMC suppression at bit 37, a second unit-mask byte in bits 40 through 47, transactional states at bits 32 and 33, and adaptive modes at bit 34 for event select and bit 32 for fixed control."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_FIXED_BITS_STRIDE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_FIXED_0_KERNEL","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_FIXED_0_USER","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_FIXED_0_ANYTHREAD","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_FIXED_0_ENABLE_PMI","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_FIXED_0_RDPMC_USER_DISABLE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_FIXED_3_METRICS_CLEAR","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_FIXED_BITS_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::intel_fixed_bits_by_idx"],"text":"Fixed-counter control uses four bits per counter. Within each group the low positions mean kernel, user, any-thread and PMI enable, with user RDPMC disable carried high at bit 33. A separate clear control lives at bit 2 for the metrics fixed counter. A combined mask gathers the allowed fixed bits, and a helper derives a counter group by shifting the base pattern by index times stride."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_EVENTSEL_INT_CORE_ENABLE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_EVENTSEL_GUESTONLY","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_EVENTSEL_HOSTONLY","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_EVENTSEL_HOST_GUEST_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_EVENTSEL_INT_CORE_SEL_SHIFT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_EVENTSEL_INT_CORE_SEL_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_EVENTSEL_EVENT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_ARCH_EVENT_MASK"],"text":"AMD event select adds interrupt-to-core enable at bit 36, guest-only and host-only at bits 40 and 41 with a combined host-guest mask, a 4 bit interrupt destination selector at shift 37, an extended event code joining the low event byte with a high nibble at bits 32 through 35, and an arch mask joining event and unit mask."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_L3_SLICE_SHIFT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_L3_SLICE_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_L3_SLICEID_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_L3_THREAD_SHIFT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_L3_THREAD_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_L3_F19H_THREAD_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_L3_EN_ALL_CORES","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_L3_EN_ALL_SLICES","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_L3_COREID_SHIFT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_L3_COREID_MASK"],"text":"AMD L3 modifiers place slice selection at shift 48 with full and identifier masks, thread selection at shift 56 with a wide mask and a narrow family-specific mask, all-cores enable at bit 47, all-slices enable at bit 46, and core identifier at shift 42 with a 3 bit mask."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::X86_RAW_EVENT_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::X86_ALL_EVENT_FLAGS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_RAW_EVENT_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_RAW_EVENT_MASK_NB","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_PERFMON_V2_EVENTSEL_EVENT_NB","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_PERFMON_V2_EVENTSEL_UMASK_NB","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_PERFMON_V2_RAW_EVENT_MASK_NB","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_PERFMON_V2_ENABLE_UMC","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_PERFMON_V2_EVENTSEL_EVENT_UMC","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_PERFMON_V2_EVENTSEL_RDWRMASK_UMC","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_PERFMON_V2_RAW_EVENT_MASK_UMC"],"text":"Raw-event and flag masks are unions of event-select fields. The generic raw mask keeps event, unit mask, edge, invert and compare; the full flag set adds any-thread, pin, and transactional bits. AMD variants extend these for northbridge and version two, including separate event and unit-mask pieces for northbridge and event plus read-write mask pieces plus an enable bit for unified memory controller."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_NUM_COUNTERS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_NUM_COUNTERS_CORE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_NUM_COUNTERS_NB","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_UNHALTED_CORE_CYCLES_SEL","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_UNHALTED_CORE_CYCLES_UMASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_UNHALTED_CORE_CYCLES_INDEX","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_UNHALTED_CORE_CYCLES_PRESENT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_BRANCH_MISSES_RETIRED","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTS_COUNT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::PEBS_DATACFG_MEMINFO","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::PEBS_DATACFG_GP","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::PEBS_DATACFG_XMMS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::PEBS_DATACFG_LBRS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::PEBS_DATACFG_CNTR","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::PEBS_DATACFG_METRICS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::PEBS_DATACFG_LBR_SHIFT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::PEBS_DATACFG_CNTR_SHIFT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::PEBS_DATACFG_CNTR_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::PEBS_DATACFG_FIX_SHIFT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::PEBS_DATACFG_FIX_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::PEBS_UPDATE_DS_SW"],"text":"AMD supplies four counters generally, six for cores and four for northbridge. The unhalted core-cycles preset uses select 0x3c with zero unit mask at index zero and a presence bit derived from that index; branch-misses-retired is event six within seven counted presets. PEBS data config enables memory info, general registers, SSE state, branch records, counters and metrics in bits zero through five, with branch-record shift 24, counter shift 32 and 16 bit mask, fixed shift 48 and 8 bit mask, plus a software DS update request at bit 63."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid10_eax","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid10_eax.anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid10_ebx","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid10_ebx.anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid10_edx","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid10_edx.anon_1"],"text":"Three CPUID unions expose perfmon enumeration, each offering a bit-field view and a whole-word view. The EAX form carries version, general counter count, counter width and mask length in bytes. The EBX form carries seven absence flags for standard presets. The EDX form carries fixed-counter count in five bits, fixed width in eight bits, reserved gaps and an any-thread deprecation flag."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EXT_LEAF","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_NUM_COUNTER_LEAF","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_ACR_LEAF","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_PEBS_CAP_LEAF","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_PEBS_COUNTER_LEAF","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::EXT_PERFMON_DEBUG_FEATURES","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CPUID_FEATURES"],"text":"CPUID leaf numbers are fixed: extended perfmon at 0x23 with subleaves one for counter count, two for auto-reload, four for PEBS capabilities and five for PEBS counters; extended debug features at 0x80000022; and sampling features at 0x8000001b."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid35_eax","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid35_eax.anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid35_ebx","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid35_ebx.anon_1"],"text":"The 0x23 EAX union reports which subleaves exist through leaf, counter, reload, events and two PEBS presence bits plus reserved space. The EBX union reports support for second unit mask, equality mode and user RDPMC disable plus reserved space. Both also expose a full-word view."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid28_eax","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid28_eax.anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid28_ebx","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid28_ebx.anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid28_ecx","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid28_ecx.anon_1"],"text":"Branch-record enumeration uses three unions with field and whole views. EAX gives an eight bit depth mask, deep sleep reset and linear-address behavior. EBX gives privilege filtering, branch filtering and call-stack mode. ECX gives mispredict, timed, branch-type and a four bit branch-counter capability plus reserved space."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid_0x80000022_ebx","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid_0x80000022_ebx.anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::x86_pmu_capability"],"text":"The 0x80000022 EBX union packs core counter count in four bits, branch-stack size in six bits, data-fabric counter count in six bits and memory-controller counter count in six bits. A capability record aggregates version, general and fixed counts and widths, an events mask with length, and single-bit flags for PEBS on EPT and mediated virtualization."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_FIXED_RDPMC_BASE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_FIXED_RDPMC_METRICS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_FIXED_INSTRUCTIONS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_FIXED_CPU_CYCLES","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_FIXED_REF_CYCLES","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_MSK_FIXED_REF_CYCLES","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_FIXED_SLOTS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_MSK_FIXED_SLOTS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_FIXED_BTS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_FIXED_VLBR","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_FIXED_VLBR_EVENT"],"text":"User RDPMC encodings set bit 30 for fixed counters and bit 29 for metrics. Fixed logical indices for instructions, cycles, reference cycles and slots are the fixed base plus zero through three, with reference and slots also having single-bit masks at their indices. Branch-trace-store sits at fixed base plus fifteen, virtual branch records reuse the frozen-branch bit number as its index, and its event code is 0x1b00."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::use_fixed_pseudo_encoding"],"text":"A small predicate classifies a 64 bit event code as fixed pseudo encoding exactly when its lowest eight bits are all clear."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_METRIC_BASE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_TD_RETIRING","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_TD_BAD_SPEC","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_TD_FE_BOUND","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_TD_BE_BOUND","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_TD_HEAVY_OPS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_TD_BR_MISPREDICT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_TD_FETCH_LAT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_TD_MEM_BOUND","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_METRIC_END","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_MSK_TOPDOWN","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_SLOTS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_METRIC_RETIRING","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_METRIC_BAD_SPEC","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_METRIC_FE_BOUND","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_METRIC_BE_BOUND","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_METRIC_HEAVY_OPS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_METRIC_BR_MISPREDICT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_METRIC_FETCH_LAT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_METRIC_MEM_BOUND","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_METRIC_MAX","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_METRIC_NUM","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_CFG_METRIC_CLEAR_BIT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_TD_CFG_METRIC_CLEAR","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_OTHER_TOPDOWN_BITS"],"text":"Top-down metrics start at fixed base plus sixteen with eight consecutive indices for retiring, bad speculation, front-end bound, back-end bound, heavy operations, branch mispredict, fetch latency and memory bound; the metric end equals the last of these. A top-down mask joins all eight metric bits with the slots fixed bit, and a helper clears one selected bit from that set. Slot and metric event codes are 0x0400 and 0x8000 through 0x8700 in steps of 0x100, the maximum equals the last metric, the count is eight, and metric clear is bit zero."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::is_metric_idx","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::is_topdown_idx"],"text":"One helper reports whether an index falls inside the eight metric slots by unsigned range check from the metric base, and another reports top-down membership when either that metric check holds or the index equals the slots fixed index."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_COND_CHG","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_BUFFER_OVF_BIT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_BUFFER_OVF","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_UNC_OVF","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_ASIF","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_COUNTERS_FROZEN","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_LBRS_FROZEN_BIT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_LBRS_FROZEN","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_TRACE_TOPAPMI_BIT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_TRACE_TOPAPMI","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_ARCH_PEBS_THRESHOLD_BIT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_ARCH_PEBS_THRESHOLD","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_STATUS_PERF_METRICS_OVF_BIT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::GLOBAL_CTRL_EN_PERF_METRICS"],"text":"Global status packs condition change at bit 63, data-buffer overflow at 62, uncore overflow at 61, adaptive-state at 60, frozen counters at 59, frozen branch records at 58, trace top-apmi at 55, architectural PEBS threshold at 54 and metrics overflow at bit 48. Global control enables metrics also at bit 48."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::pebs_basic","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::pebs_meminfo","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::pebs_meminfo.anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::pebs_meminfo.anon_1.anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::pebs_gprs","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::pebs_xmm","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::pebs_cntr_header","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_CNTR_METRICS"],"text":"Legacy PEBS layouts start with a basic header of format group, retire latency, format size, instruction pointer, applicable counters and timestamp. Memory info holds address, auxiliary, a latency union that is either a single value or split instruction and cache latencies with padding, plus transactional tuning. General registers cover flags, IP and all integer registers; SSE state holds two words per sixteen registers; a counter header holds general, fixed, metrics and reserved counts; the metrics selector value is three."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_index","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_index.anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_header","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_header.anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_header.anon_1.anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_basic","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_aux"],"text":"Architectural PEBS index packs reserved gaps with a 23 bit write offset, full and enable flags and a 23 bit threshold plus a whole-word view. The record header packs size, 64 bit mode, continuation, counter selector, branch-record count, vector-extension presence for SSE, upper YMM, opmask, upper ZMM and high ZMM, general-register, auxiliary and basic presence, with reserved space. Basic state holds IP, applicable counters, timestamp, retire latency and valid flag. Auxiliary state holds address, auxiliary value, instruction and cache latencies and transactional tuning with reserved words."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_gprs","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_xer_header","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PEBS_LBR_NAN","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PEBS_LBR_NUM_8","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PEBS_LBR_NUM_16","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PEBS_LBR_NUM_VAR","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PEBS_BASE_LBR_ENTRIES","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_lbr_header","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_cntr_header"],"text":"Architectural PEBS general registers add a shadow-stack pointer to the legacy integer set. Extended-state header carries an xstate bitmap. Branch-record count encodings are zero for none, one for eight, two for sixteen and three for variable, with eight base entries. A branch header carries control, depth and last-exception source, destination and info. A counter header mirrors the legacy split of general, fixed, metrics and reserved."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_AVAIL","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_FETCHSAM","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_OPSAM","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_RDWROPCNT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_OPCNT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_BRNTRGT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_OPCNTEXT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_RIPINVALIDCHK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_OPBRNFUSE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_FETCHCTLEXTD","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_OPDATA4","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_ZEN4","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_OPLDLAT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_DIS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_FETCHLAT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_BIT63_FILTER","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_STRMST_RMTSOCKET","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_OPDTLBPGSIZE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_CAPS_DEFAULT"],"text":"Sampling capabilities are single bits for availability, fetch sampling, operation sampling, read-write operation count, operation count, branch target, extended operation count, invalid-RIP check, fused-branch handling, extended fetch control, fourth operation data, Zen4 features, load latency, dispatch, fetch latency, bit-63 filtering, remote-socket streaming and TLB page-size detail. The default set joins availability with fetch and operation sampling."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBSCTL","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBSCTL_LVT_OFFSET_VALID","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBSCTL_LVT_OFFSET_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_L3MISSONLY","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_RAND_EN","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_VAL","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_ENABLE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_CNT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_MAX_CNT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_2_DIS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_2_FETCHLAT_FILTER","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_2_FETCHLAT_FILTER_SHIFT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_2_EXCL_RIP_63_EQ_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_2_EXCL_RIP_63_EQ_0"],"text":"Sampling control lives at 0x1cc with a valid flag at bit 8 and a four bit LVT offset mask. Fetch control provides miss-only filtering at bit 59, random enable at 57, valid at 49, enable at 48, a count field and a maximum-count field. Second fetch control provides dispatch suppression at bit zero, a four bit fetch-latency filter at shift one, and exclusion controls for RIP bit 63 equal to one or zero."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_FIXED","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_METRIC_BASE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_METRIC_END","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_MSK_TOPDOWN","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::intel_fixed_bits_by_idx","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_FIXED_BITS_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_UNHALTED_CORE_CYCLES_PRESENT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::X86_RAW_EVENT_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::AMD64_PERFMON_V2_RAW_EVENT_MASK_NB","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_OTHER_TOPDOWN_BITS"],"text":"Logical numbering is arithmetic: fixed roles are small offsets from the fixed base, metrics are consecutive from the metric base ending at memory-bound, and masks are single bits or unions at those positions. Fixed-control placement scales by stride, presence bits shift by preset index, and raw or version-two masks are strict unions of their named event-select pieces, so adding a piece can only widen the kept field set."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::pebs_meminfo","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::pebs_meminfo.anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::cpuid10_eax","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_index","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_OTHER_TOPDOWN_BITS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_CNT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::IBS_FETCH_MAX_CNT"],"text":"Several layouts invite misreading: the memory-info latency union has generation-dependent meaning, CPUID and PEBS bit-fields assume the compiler layout and little-endian order, high single-bit shifts require 64 bit arithmetic, the top-down exclusion helper complements only within the top-down mask, and fetch count versus maximum count share one control word with different halves."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_index","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_header","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::arch_pebs_basic"],"text":"The architectural PEBS index word describes buffer-fill state through enable, current write position, threshold and full indications, while the record header continuation flag and basic valid bit describe whether a record continues a sequence and whether its retire latency is meaningful. The fragments show the state fields but not transition or interrupt sequencing."}],"index_id":"99dbddb713e8d299bd55ae3ea6f9df9103f2fe09352557dba05a5a735dfe6c48","lane":52,"pass":1,"prefix_sha256":"90fbc6904033e42000ae762f7e22713ee62f438dcdedfc4bd7328bc76c81714c","prompt_sha256":"70cb61acdfe8a5e731b0c44a86dfbd6883035c0ec13dbeba08e5e693d72e9104","schema":"lx.extract.v1","sids_read":["arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_MAX_GENERIC","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_MAX_FIXED","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::INTEL_PMC_IDX_FIXED","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::X86_PMC_IDX_MAX","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_PERFCTR0","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_PERFCTR1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL0","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::MSR_ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL1","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_EVENT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_UMASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_USR","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_OS","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_EDGE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_PIN_CONTROL","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_INT","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_ANY","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_ENABLE","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_INV","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_CMASK","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_BR_CNTR","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_EQ","arch/x86/include/asm/perf_event.h::ARCH_PERFMON_EVENTSEL_RDPMC_USER_DISABLE","ar